    "result_text": "The full suite passed (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; the other files are helpers.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `telephoneDisplay` as a read-only, display-only field derived from the stored E.164 `telephone`, keeping `telephone` raw.\n\nThree small, isolated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` (read-only string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-method helper that renders E.164 for humans: `+61412345678 \u2192 +61 412 345 678` (country code, a space, national digits grouped in threes via a regex). It leaves non-E.164 input unchanged. New file with no surrounding class complexity.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line wiring `telephoneDisplay` to `TelephoneDisplay.display(owner.getTelephone())`, matching the existing pattern used for the other derived fields.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** the formatting logic lives in a brand-new, zero-context class (WMC_other = 0), so the heavy behaviour carries the minimum multiplier. The only edit to an existing function is a single annotation line on the mapper interface method (CC = 1), and the schema/DTO change is generated rather than hand-written. No existing function grew in complexity.",
